# ── Model provider ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Which model provider to use:
#   "anthropic" (default) — Anthropic API; requires ANTHROPIC_API_KEY below.
#   "session"             — no API key: generations are written as request files
#                           to the outbox and fulfilled by a Claude Code /
#                           claude.ai session (covered by your Claude
#                           subscription). See docs/DECISIONS.md D-008.
#   "mock"                — tests/dev only; output is watermarked, never
#                           presented as real analysis.
TALENTOS_MODEL_PROVIDER=anthropic

# Outbox directory for the "session" provider's file handoff.
TALENTOS_SESSION_OUTBOX=./data/session-outbox

# Anthropic API key. Server-side only; never exposed to the client.
# With no key set, every AI feature shows a "provider not configured" state —
# nothing is faked.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Model override (default: claude-opus-5)
TALENTOS_MODEL=claude-opus-5

# ── Database ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SQLite database file. Default: ./data/talentos.db (created on first run).
# Back up by copying this one file.
TALENTOS_DATABASE_PATH=./data/talentos.db

# ── Candidate discovery provider (people search, D-010) ──────────────────────
# "talent-xray" (default) — live people-only discovery through the two Talent
# X-Ray Programmable Search engines (Discover tab). Link-out to the engines'
# own hosted results page needs no key and is always on (D-034). The JSON API
# provider below is optional: Google closed the Custom Search JSON API to new
# customers and ends it on 2027-01-01 (D-033), so leave the key blank unless
# you are a grandfathered customer. "none" disables the API path. Result pages
# are never fetched, only results you explicitly save are stored, and saved
# snippets are labeled unverified source evidence — never resume content.
TALENTOS_DISCOVERY_PROVIDER=talent-xray
TALENTOS_GOOGLE_CSE_KEY=
# Engine overrides (default: the live Talent X-Ray engines)
# TALENTOS_CSE_CORE_CX=a157d37906e1141cc
# TALENTOS_CSE_REACH_CX=918bc00e18d0c46e5

# Open-web search (Brave), used when TALENTOS_DISCOVERY_PROVIDER=brave. Its own
# index rather than somebody else's results resold against their terms, and
# commercial use is permitted. Nothing calls out without the key.
# Until `pnpm probe:search` has been run against a real key, every row in
# OPERATOR_SUPPORT says `unverified` and the settings page says how many: an
# operator the index silently drops turns a precise query into a broad one, and
# the rows still look like answers.
TALENTOS_BRAVE_SEARCH_KEY=

# ── Declared profile links (Wave H) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Opt-in only. When set to "1", the candidate page can read the addresses a
# person listed on a profile they control, through that platform's own public
# JSON API: one person, one click, never in bulk. "mock" is for tests and
# makes no network call. Unset means the app never calls out and says so.
# Nothing is stored until you keep a specific address.
# TALENTOS_PROFILES_GITHUB=1
# Optional. A free GitHub personal access token raises the rate limit from 60
# to 5,000 requests an hour. Sent as a bearer header, never returned or
# stored. No scopes are needed for public profile data.
# TALENTOS_GITHUB_TOKEN=
# Keybase proofs are cryptographic, so they are the one source that earns the
# reciprocal tier. Keyless. Keybase has been largely dormant since 2020.
# TALENTOS_PROFILES_KEYBASE=1

# ── Reading pages (D-082) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Off, and it takes TWO switches. Setting either one on its own changes
# nothing: reading stays off, and the settings page names whichever is missing.
#
# What turning both on WOULD do: a page an engine returned can be opened and
# read for the people on it, behind the policy gate in `src/lib/fetch/` — the
# host's own robots.txt, the source registry, one request at a time per host,
# a size cap and a per-run budget, and a hard stop at a sign-in wall, a paywall
# or a bot check. The page is read and dropped: the claim and the address are
# kept, the page is not, and nothing reaches the database until you save a
# person.
#
# What it would NOT do, at any setting. It does not crawl — one address in,
# one page out, and no link is followed. It does not get past a challenge, a
# sign-in or a paywall; it stops and says which one it saw. It does not read a
# host the registry refuses or hands off, and a redirect onto one is refused at
# the hop rather than inherited. It does not read anything in bulk, and it does
# not widen the registry: a row whose basis is `assumed` stays assumed until a
# human reads that host's terms and records the date on the row.
TALENTOS_FETCH=off
# The second switch, and the one people forget. A URL a site owner can open to
# find out who is asking and how to make it stop; it is sent in the User-Agent
# of every request this makes. It has to be a page that exists and that you
# read, because a fetcher nobody can complain to is one nobody can ask to stop.
# Blank means reading stays off however TALENTOS_FETCH is set.
TALENTOS_FETCH_CONTACT=
# Optional. This install's own public origin, so the reader refuses to fetch
# itself.
# TALENTOS_PUBLIC_ORIGIN=

# ── Public registries (Wave E, D-032) ────────────────────────────────────────
# Opt-in only. "1" lets the candidate page query the public CMS NPI Registry
# (https://npiregistry.cms.hhs.gov, no key) by name/state or NPI; you pick
# the record by hand and an allow-listed snapshot is stored as
# "registry-matched · CMS NPPES" — identity and taxonomy, never a private
# contact. "mock" is for tests. Unset: nothing calls out; the card shows a
# link to the registry's own search page instead.
TALENTOS_REGISTRY_NPPES=

# ── Research provider (general information environment, D-010/D-013) ────────
# Separate boundary from candidate discovery: profession/company/market and
# AUDIENCE research (personas before outreach). Values:
#   "session" — a Claude session performs the web search via the same outbox
#               file handoff as the session model provider (no key)
#   "mock"    — tests only; watermarked fixture findings, never real research
#   "none"    — no backend; personas and outreach stop with an honest error
# Unset: follows the model provider (session → session, mock → mock, else
# none). The people-only engines above are deliberately not accepted here.
TALENTOS_RESEARCH_PROVIDER=
